From 8f0edfa665dfc37f8a813e78a06fa68d2d7ecf13 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:47:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Light from torches and spells: the new look lights the ground
 around a Fireball, a torch and a heal
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Under the new look (`worldLook 1`) torches, lamps and spells now light the world around them per
pixel, WoW Forever's secondary lights in a Classic style. 1.12's own point lights, three a draw
summed per vertex, are kept exactly; this is a second table on top, and the classic look has none.

- Torches, braziers, lamps and lit rooms (every authored point light benilla already reads: M2
  lights on props and carried items, WMO MOLT omni lights, glowing objects) cast a warm pool of
  about 7 to 10 yd with a slow, small flicker for a flame. They come up through dusk (17:00 to
  21:00), burn full at night and are all but out by day (6 % at noon); inside a building, 70 %.
- A missile carries a light of its spell's colour (its Basin Battle trail's, else its school's:
  holy gold, fire orange, nature green, frost ice blue, shadow violet, arcane pink-violet), so the
  ground under a Fireball's path turns orange. An impact flashes brighter and shorter (0.5 s); a
  heal glows softer and longer on the hero (1.4 s); a cast glows on its caster while drawn up; an
  aura with a visual breathes faintly on its unit; a ground area glows over its circle.

`benilla_world::look::lights` ranks every candidate within 100 yd of the camera by brightness
against distance and packs up to 24 into the shared light buffer after the point table (row 20 `.y`
the count): the best 16 lit, the other 8 slots fading out, so a light entering or leaving the set
fades over 0.4 s instead of popping, and one whose entity went fades where it was. No per-frame
allocation once warm. `terrain.wgsl`, `wow_model.wgsl` and `static_gx.wgsl` add each light as
`texture · rgb · (1 − (d/r)²)² · wrap(N·L)` inside the final clamp, before the fog; not on unlit,
additive, Mod or Mod2x batches or the sky shell. A pixel loops over the live entries only (none
under the classic look); an out-of-range light costs two storage reads and a distance test.
`benilla-app`'s `look_lights` hangs the spell lights from the missile spawns, the GO hit lists, the
arrivals, the kit edges and the DynamicObject creates, all in `PostUpdate` through commands.

Every number is in `look::lights::tune`. `looklights <scale>` (0 to 10, `tuned` to go back) scales
them all live, for tuning on film. benilla's own; no reference behaviour.

Tuned after the first night films, where a lamp post cast no pool you could see and even `looklights
3` moved Goldshire's frame by under a level in 255: torches burn at 2.1 (from 0.7, the dimmest
authored lamp at 1.3), missiles at 2.7 (from 0.9) and impacts 3.0, heals 1.6, casts 1.0, areas 1.2
and auras 0.5. Every authored light casts a full 10 yd torch pool whatever its authored reach; only
Basin Battle's glowing objects (a planted arrow's 4 yd light) stay a small find-me glow. A look
light multiplies the texture no darker than 0.15 a channel, so Elwynn's near-black night ground
takes the light's own hue rather than nothing. A cool light (Frostbolt) leans 30% toward white and
burns 1.5 times brighter, to show on warm ground, and every spell light's colour is taken at full
peak. With the camera outdoors a building's interior lights rank at 30%, so the street's lamps and
the spells win the 16 slots. `looklights` reaches 10.
